---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Page not found"
  description="The requested page could not be found. Return to the church software directory, categories or practical guides."
  noindex
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">404</p>
      <h1>That page could not be found</h1>
      <p class="measure">
        The address may have changed, or the page may not exist. Try one of the
        main sections below.
      </p>
      <div class="cluster">
        <a class="button" href="/software/">Browse software</a>
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="/categories/">View categories</a>
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="/guides/">Read guides</a>
      </div>
      <h2>Find the right next step</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        Start with the directory if you already know the type of tool you need.
        Browse categories to understand a particular operational problem, or use
        the guides for questions about pricing, Gift Aid, data and choosing a
        responsible starting point. If you followed an old product link, use
        the directory search to check whether the current profile has moved.
      </p>
      <p class="measure">
        Church Software UK records supplier-published information alongside
        independent assessment and questions still to settle. It does not use an
        overall product score, so the most useful route depends on the decision
        your church is making. You can also read our methodology to understand
        how sources, corrections and editorial independence are handled.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/methodology/">Read the research methodology</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
